 "learning_loop": {
  "setup": "Split units (clusters of copies) are split 50/50 into pool and test at random, 5 seeds. The officer labels k photos from the pool, one photo per copy group, in random order; the head is refit on the phone (adapt from ml/train_eval.py: cross-entropy + prior_strength/2 x squared distance to the starting head) and the labelled photos join the familiarity reference. Familiarity is the app's rule: 10 nearest stored rows within the cutoff, OR the nearest officer-labelled photo within ood.local_nearest_cutoff (0.494). Threshold, cutoffs and temperature stay as shipped. Test photos: the other half; each copy group counts once. Labels are the dataset authors' folder labels, standing in for the officer. ood.local_nearest_cutoff was chosen on 40% of the Ugandan copy clusters (results/familiarity_rule.json), which are included here; that file has the numbers on the other 60% only.",
