 "plain_summary": [
  "Test set: 3,192 coffee-leaf photos from farms in Uganda (healthy, rust, Phoma; 1,351 distinct leaves after grouping copies), never used for training; one setting of the app's familiarity rule (ood.local_nearest_cutoff) was chosen on 40% of the copy clusters (results/familiarity_rule.json), which this loop includes.",
  "The 'not sure' check protects the count in a new country: if forced to answer, the shipped model (v3-2026-10-03-lab+field+other) is right on only 43% of Ugandan photos; the app instead sends 93% of them to the officer and calls only 3% of healthy leaves a problem.",
  "With officer labels the tool learns the new country: after 50 labels it answers 33% of photos, 90% correctly; after 100, 47% (93% correct). Right if forced goes from 43% to 81% after 50 labels.",
  "Why it opens: a photo also counts as familiar when its nearest officer-labelled photo is close. With the previous rule (10 nearest stored photos only) the tool answered only 8% after 50 labels and 9% after 100.",
  "Limit: Phoma is the look-alike. After 100 labels the tool names rust on 47% of rust leaves and Phoma on 32% of Phoma leaves; healthy leaves called a problem: 1%.",
  "Data checks: 102 empty files dropped, 1,411 byte-identical extra copies grouped, 28 photos dropped because a near-identical copy sits in another class folder (phoma vs rust). Photos are 256 x 256 close-ups of leaves on the plant."
 ],
 "limits_and_next_steps": [
  {
   "limit": "The 'not sure' check opens only with officer labels: with none, the app answers 7% of Ugandan photos; after 50 labels 33%, after 100 47%, so the officer still sees most photos early on. The setting that opens it (ood.local_nearest_cutoff) was chosen on 40% of these copy clusters.",
   "next_step": "Report answered and correct of answered on the first 200 officer-labelled Kenyan pilot photos (sealed); who: ML lead; metric: answered and correct of answered after 50 and 100 labels; when: first pilot month."
  },
  {
   "limit": "Uganda, not Kenya: photos come from farms in Uganda (Soroti University team), not from Kenyan farms.",
   "next_step": "Keep the first 200 officer-labelled Kenyan pilot photos aside as a Kenyan test set; who: the team with the co-op extension officer; metric: share answered and correct of answered; when: first pilot month."
  },
  {
   "limit": "Coffee species not stated in the dataset description (Uganda grows both robusta and arabica).",
   "next_step": "Record species per plot with pilot photos and report results by species; who: the officer at each plot visit; metric: correct of answered by species; when: from the first pilot visit."
  },
  {
   "limit": "Photo style: close-ups of single leaves on the plant, outdoors in daylight, stored at 256 x 256 pixels (checked by eye on about 70 photos; a few show soil behind the leaf, so some may be fallen or held leaves). The phone sees full-resolution photos framed by a relay farmer.",
   "next_step": "On the first 100 pilot photos, compare share answered on full photos vs the same photos cut to 256 px; who: the team; metric: share answered and correct of answered; when: pilot week 1."
  },
  {
   "limit": "Copies: the dataset mixes rotated, flipped, brightness-adjusted and byte-identical copies (1,411 byte-identical extra files). We group copies by image similarity (1,351 copy groups from 3,192 photos); copies that were also cropped or strongly brightened can escape the grouping, so a few near-copies may sit on both sides of the learning-loop split. The coarser-grouping runs show how much this matters.",
   "next_step": "Ask the dataset authors for the original (before augmentation) file list; who: the team by email; metric: rerun with exact groups and compare; when: after the challenge."
  },
  {
   "limit": "Labels: folder labels from the dataset authors stand in for the officer. 28 photos had a near-identical copy in another class folder (phoma vs rust) and were dropped; some photos in the Phoma folder show rust-like orange spots, so some label noise likely remains.",
   "next_step": "Have the extension officer relabel a random 100 Ugandan photos and report agreement with the folder labels; who: co-op officer; metric: share of agreement; when: pilot week 1."
  },
  {
   "limit": "Learning-step strength (prior_strength), answer threshold and familiarity cutoff are the shipped values; none was tuned on Ugandan photos.",
